[0.592,"o","\u001b[H\u001b[3G1. \u001b[1mAC3 — how are ids compared for the tie-break?\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6G- Plain \u001b[15Gtring order (\u001b[38;5;153mINV-10\u001b[39m before\u001b[42G\u001b[38;5;153mINV-2\u001b[39m),\u001b[50Gnatural/numeric\u001b[66Gorder\u001b[72G(\u001b[38;5;153mINV-2\u001b[79G\u001b[39mbefore\r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;153mINV-10\u001b[39m),\u001b[17Gor\u001b[20G\u001b[38;5;153mlocaleCompare\u001b[34G\u001b[39m(locale-dependent)?\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6G- What changes: the comparator and the test fixture\u001b[58Gids\u001b[62GI\u001b[64Guse\u001b[68Gto\u001b[71Gcheck\u001b[77Gties.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B2.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mAC1 — what is “the current date” when \u001b[38;5;153m--today\u001b[39m is omitted?\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B-\u001b[8GUTC date\u001b[17G(\u001b[38;5;153mnew D\u001b[24Gt\u001b[26G().toISOString().slice(0, 10)\u001b[39m,\u001b[57Gas\u001b[60G\u001b[38;5;153maging\u001b[66G\u001b[39mdoes),\u001b[73Gor\u001b[76Gthe\u001b[80Gmachine’s\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B \u001b[8Glocal c\u001b[16Glendar date?\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6G- What changes: which invoices are in the list when the local\u001b[68Gdate\u001b[73Gand\u001b[77GUTC\u001b[81Gdate\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B \u001b[8Gdiffer; a test around a fixed clock would assert\u001b[57Gthe chosen one.\u001b[73G(I\u001b[76Greco\u001b[81Gmend UTC,\r\u001b[7C\u001b[1Bt\u001b[10G mat\u001b[15Gh \u001b[38;5;153maging\u001b[39m.)\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B3.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mAC1 — what happens with a bad \u001b[38;5;153m--today\u001b[39m?\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B-\u001b[8GExamples:\u001b[18G\u001b[38;5;153m--today\u001b[39m with no value, \u001b[38;5;153m--today 15-11-2026\u001b[39m,\u001b[61Gor an impossible date like\u001b[K\r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;153m2026-02-30\u001b[39m.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6G- Should it exit with an error and no CSV\u001b[48G(and\u001b[53Gif\u001b[56Gso,\u001b[60Gwhich\u001b[66Gexit\